WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.219
Stick around to the end of the video, where
we’ll look at all of the connections between

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:06.630
Mordeo and the Native American legend it’s
based on, The Wendigo.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.980
This video is sponsored by CryptTV.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.839
[Intro]

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:15.659
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:15.659 --> 00:00:19.440
In this video, I’ll be breaking down everything
you missed in Offering, the new episode of

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.840
Mordeo on CryptTV.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.210
For those who aren’t aware, Mordeo is a
serialization of the 2017 Crypt short film

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.230
of the same name, in which a cannibal in the
woods is transformed into a monster controlled

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.320
by the Mordeo.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.660
We later find out in a Crypt announcement
video that the creature who appeared in that

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.110
short is merely a scout, a proxy of the Queen.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.660
So the new episode opens, as many Crypt productions
do, with a little bit of gore.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.190
This character Dan, gets his fingers chopped
off by a masked man simply known as The Butcher.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.820
At first I assumed that the woman hiding out
behind the tree, Linda, was his girlfriend

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:50.820
or something.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.350
However, Dan has a ring on his finger, and
she does not.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.489
We’ll see if that actually ends up being
a significant part of the story or if it’s

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.860
just an extra detail.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.960
The Butcher is carrying a book and a newspaper
with him and both contain important details.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.449
He starts by referencing the book, which we
can quickly see based on the art style, is

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:09.320
the Crypt Tome, the book most prominently
featured in Sunny Family Cult. that contains

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.830
rituals men may use to turn themselves into
monsters.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:16.040
The Butcher uses the book to find the ritual
site, and carry out the ritual.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.080
He is able to get the Queen Mordeo to appear,
and seems to be excited to transform into

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.560
a monster, yelling out things like, “I’m
ready” and “please make me one of you.”

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.869
However, things don’t go as he expected.

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:31.130
The Queen bites off three of his fingers on
his right hand, the same fingers that he removed

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.900
from Dan at the beginning of the episode.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.700
It is as it was told by the victim in the
original Mordeo short film.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.250
“...there’s a price to pay for eating
flesh in these woods.”

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.100
So The Butcher is cursed with permanent finger
guns for life, which is really only another

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.950
minute or so because the Queen Mordeo snaps
his neck.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.650
The butcher appears to have followed the ritual,
so why wasn’t he turned into a monster?

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.940
Let’s look back at the book.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:57.950
It shows imagery of human flesh, along with
an open mouth and the words hunger, desperation

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:58.950
and offering.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.240
There’s also an illustration of the hooded
scout from the original short film that this

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.540
series based on, so let’s look there for
more clues.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.490
That one also has a cannibal eating flesh,
but in his case, he appears to be eating in

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:10.790
order to survive.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.090
Listen to this dialogue.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.520
“You were hungry.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.830
There’s no shame in that.”

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.920
The Butcher in the new episode isn’t doing
it because he’s hungry, he’s doing it

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.340
to try to become a monster.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.380
Hunger, desperation and offering.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.470
These are the requirements that must be met
in order for the transformation to take place,

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.040
just as Roger had to meet certain requirements
in the third season of Sunny Family Cult.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.260
That wraps up the mystery of The Butcher,
but we still don’t know why the other two

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.690
human characters, Dan and Linda, are out in
the woods as well.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.860
When in doubt when watching Crypt TV stuff,
you always gotta look for paper.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.080
Speaking of which, you should sign up for
the Crypt newsletter.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.060
I mean, it doesn’t actually come on paper
it’s an email with updates on the Crypt

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.140
monster universe, special access merch drops
and insider info.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.629
It’s free, just look for my link in the
description.

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:58.209
Anyway, the newspaper headline tells us what
we need to know going forward into this season.

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:04.780
There are three missing girl scouts, Angela,
Nancy and… uhh the other one.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.560
Jen.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.440
I told you.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.450
Always look for papers.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.980
This is just pure speculation, but Nancy looks
like she could possibly be related to Linda,

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.810
the girl we saw hiding from The Butcher.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.930
My guess is that Linda and Dan are out searching
for the missing girls.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.730
The name of the newspaper is The Mohawk Ledger,
which ties into another Crypt series, Mohawk,

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.879
which takes place in a tiny New York town
in a modern setting.

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:31.209
However, Mordeo takes place about 40 years
before that.

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:35.550
If you pause on the newspaper right before
the blood hits it, you can see the date, October

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.510
29th 1979.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.780
That also places this just two days before
Halloween, which may or may not be significant

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.670
once we get into those later episodes.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.710
In addition to the search for those missing
girls, there’s also another clue pointing

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.180
towards a possible crossover with another
Crypt TV franchise.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.730
This symbol carved on the fallen tree doesn’t
match up with the symbol of Mordeo, but rather,

00:03:54.730 --> 00:04:00.349
the icon of The Birch, another forest dwelling
monster and a protector of good children against

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:01.349
evil.

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:04.180
The inclusion of the Birch symbol could be
just a small promotion for The Birch, which

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.049
is getting a series of its own this year,
but it could also mean that The Birch is in

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:13.150
the same territory as Mordeo, and may appear
to the aid of the missing girls if Mordeo

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.150
comes hunting.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:19.439
If that happens, expect to see a huge showdown
between Mordeo and The Birch.

00:04:19.439 --> 00:04:22.710
Mordeo is based off of a mythological creature
known as The Wendigo.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:27.360
The Wendigo is an Algonquian legend associated
with famine, greed and cannibalism.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.470
This episode reflects those themes by introducing
The Butcher, a product of greed who is willing

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.300
to resort to cannibalism not to survive, but
simply to gain more power.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.800
The Wendigo is a demonic creature with a humanoid
form and the head of a stag.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.889
It’s hunger can never be satisfied, so it’s
always looking for new victims, making it

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:46.979
a metaphorical tale the Algonquian people
would tell their young to discourage greedy

00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:47.979
behaviour.

00:04:47.979 --> 00:04:51.550
It roams forests in the Northern Atlantic
Coast in North America, which is likely why

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.639
the territory of Mordeo resides in Mohawk,
New York.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:58.680
Tribal members would sometimes perform a ceremony
during times of famine in order to discourage

00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.900
taboo behaviours.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.839
The ceremony involved dancing around a drum
while wearing horned masks, which may have

00:05:03.839 --> 00:05:07.009
something to do with the mask worn by The
Butcher in this episode.

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:11.099
Some legends say that The Wendigo has an effect
on the entire region that it inhabits, causing

00:05:11.099 --> 00:05:13.380
evil spirits to possess locals.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.449
There are many different versions of the legend.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:19.069
The only way to find out what creepy twists
Crypt TV puts on this native folktale is to

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:24.099
subscribe to their channel and catch new episodes
of Mordeo and other Crypt Monster Universe

00:05:24.099 --> 00:05:25.599
videos every Friday.

00:05:25.599 --> 00:05:29.680
Don’t forget to sign up to that newsletter
to stay up to date on even more great content

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.449
and as always, I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:34.979
Assuming we both survive.

